  "name": "Planning Your Accessible Kitchen Project Timeline",
  "step": [
    {
      "name": "Step 1",
      "text": "Embarking on an accessible kitchen remodel is a significant undertaking that benefits greatly from a well-structured timeline. Because these projects often involve multiple trades simultaneously, careful planning ensures a smooth process and a highly functional result. Here’s a general phase-by-phase timeline you can expect:",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 1
    },
    {
      "name": "Step 2",
      "text": "**Phase 1: Initial Assessment & Design.** This is where we identify your specific needs and create a detailed layout. We'll assess current and future mobility requirements, discussing options for clear floor space, counter heights, appliance placement, and storage solutions. This phase is crucial for avoiding common mistakes like tight turning spaces or awkward reach ranges.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 2
    },
    {
      "name": "Step 3",
      "text": "**Phase 2: Demolition & Rough-Ins.** Once the design is finalized, the existing kitchen is demolished. This is followed by the",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 3
    }
  ],
